Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||07-15-2001||10:27 PM||||It has officially begun.<P>Although I did put the car up on jackstands a month ago, it has not been until I saw posts of 88Formula's 3.4l engine build that my determination and excitement overcame my busyness and most other projects that I have now actually begun to disassemble my Formula.<P>The oil and coolant are drained (well, most of it), the intake hose is removed, and the vacuum and fuel lines are disconnected.<P>Once I get my Leica (Temporary use of the Fiero Fund, but I'm selling my Minoltas to supplement it), a 3.4 block is next, along with an engine stand, and a couple of other things to supplement my tool kit. This is my first engine build, after all.... Looks like I'll be living here in Tech for a while....||||reg||4
