Z||000003||Shiner||07-16-2001||09:08 PM||||A Leica?!  Does it HAVE to be a Leica?  Can't you just get an F3 and save the rest for forced induction?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Patrick's Dad||07-17-2001||09:54 AM||||Yes, Shiner, it has to be a Leica.<P>After shooting Minolta for 18 years, I have decided to to move up. I'll miss the spot on lightmetering in "point and shoot" situations, the true 4.5fps shooting in AF, and, especially, my 16mm f2.8.<P>I looked (briefly) at the Nikon FM2. As good as it is, it doesn't have the feel of the M6, nor is it as quiet. The lensing would be, at best, a lateral move. Minolta also makes their own glass, and they've been conspiring with Leica for years. In fact, the Leica R 16mm f2.8 is the Minolta MD 16mm f2.8, and my AF 16 is actually superior to the MD 16.... It's the 35mm focal length that I'll be playing in for a while, and, if I win a lottery, the 24mm.<P>Having a Leica, by the way, does not supplant forced induction; it merely delays it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
